  "poem": "Little fly,\nThy summer\u2019s play\nMy thoughtless hand\nHas brushed away.\n\nAm not I\nA fly like thee?\nOr art not thou\nA man like me?\n\nFor I dance\nAnd drink and sing,\nTill some blind hand\nShall brush my wing.\n\nIf thought is life\nAnd strength and breath,\nAnd the want\nOf thought is death,\n\nThen am I\nA happy fly,\nIf I live,\nOr if I die.",
